    "answer": {
      "short": "Bob confused an equation with an identity. Subtract $x^2$ from both sides and solve the resulting linear equation: $x=-1$.",
      "worked": "Bob confused an equation with an identity. Corresponding coefficients must be equal when the equality holds for every value of $x$. This equation need only hold for particular values of $x$.\n\nSubtract $x^2$ from both sides and solve:\n$$\\begin{align*}3x+5&=2x+4\\\\x+1&=0\\\\x&=-1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
